      "writtenOn": "2023-07-12T18:17:52Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I want to avoid introducing new requirements into this test.\n\nSo I think what we should do is\n\n```\ninvokeGet(cfg.prop, 0);\nif (mActualStatusCode \u003d\u003d StatusCode::NOT_AVAILABLE || mActualValue.status \u003d\u003d VehiclePropertyStatus::UNAVAILABLE) {\n  continue;\n}\n```",
      "revId": "d515550cbaf868cdfe6f1ddc875a7a17f7150bdc",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "107afab7_0630927a",
        "filename": "automotive/vehicle/2.0/vts/functional/VtsHalAutomotiveVehicleV2_0TargetTest.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 211,
      "author": {
        "id": 1955624
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-07-13T11:22:52Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I don\u0027t really agree with `mActualStatusCode \u003d\u003d StatusCode::NOT_AVAILABLE`. For the certification, we expect VTS to run in a test environment that is known to be good. It\u0027s fine if the property value isn\u0027t available but the `get()` operation has to succeed.",
      "parentUuid": "668c8085_79459d33",
      "revId": "d515550cbaf868cdfe6f1ddc875a7a17f7150bdc",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "325137bc_4e4ee90c",
        "filename": "automotive/vehicle/2.0/vts/functional/VtsHalAutomotiveVehicleV2_0TargetTest.cpp",
